    "guide": "Fetch known synonym/near-duplicate concept pairs together and cross-check for divergence — they can legitimately disagree (e.g. NetIncomeLoss with ProfitLoss, Revenues with RevenueFromContractWithCustomerExcludingAssessedTax). Not every similarly-named pair is the same failure mode: some are inconsistent tagging of the same thing (reconcile to one number, or flag the divergence if it's large); others are deliberately different scopes (e.g. DebtCurrent/LongTermDebt exclude finance leases, while LongTermDebtAndFinanceLeasesCurrent/LongTermDebtAndFinanceLeasesNoncurrent include them and will consistently run a few percent higher) — present those separately with what each includes rather than collapsing them into one number. A requested concept with no matching rows in the response simply does not exist for that filing — diff the concepts you requested against the concepts actually present before answering, and call get_sec_filing_facts_catalog if a load-bearing concept came back missing rather than answering off a partial set. Report a concept as not available rather than force-fitting a value that doesn't semantically match the question."
